# TUI-DESIGN-4 §7.10 (P-D10): the TUI side of the peer registry, driven by the stub (JEVCODE_FAULT=peer:2).
# Two instances in one workspace ran to completion with ZERO mention of each other. The three surfaces: the
# status segment `2 here` (counts only — never a pid, never a path, and the FIRST thing dropped when the status
# line runs out of columns), the session-open item naming `/peers`, and `/peers` itself as a real block.
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
expect another jevcode is working in this workspace
sleep 0.3
send /peers
sleep 0.2
send \r
expect peers [·-] 
sleep 0.3
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
